  "description": "The Shift I/O 7 features our new 160mm travel 4-Bar linkage frame, with its up-to-date geometry, coupled with a Rockshox suspension package including a Yari RC 29\" Boost fork and a Super Deluxe Select R Trunnion air shock for solid Enduro-type 160mm front and rear suspension. Its internal 630Wh down tube battery supplies power to the new Shimano EP-800 motor, which features increased torque (85Nm) at lower RPMs, a smaller size and a quieter function. The Shift I/O 7 features two different wheel sizes (for M to XL-sized frames) with a 29\" front wheel and a 27.5\" rear wheel to get the best of both worlds for an unmatched riding feel. With its new Shimano XT and SLX 12-speed components, the Shift I/O 7 allows for smooth, powerful rides up or down the hills with a wide-range gear ratio to save battery life when needed and precise, crisp shifting.\nShift I/O X6 Aluminum frame for Shimano STePS EP-800 motor, 160mm travel\nRockshox Super Deluxe Select R Trunnion air shock\nRockshox Yari RC 29\" Boost, 160mm Debonair fork\nNew Shimano EP-800, 250W. / 85Nm Torque motor\nDarfon 630Wh internal battery\nShimano SW-EM800 Mode switch, Integrated speed sensor\nShimano XT M8100 12-spd, Shadow Plus rear derailleur\nShimano SLX M7100 12-spd 10-51T cassette\nShimano FC-EM600 crankset, 34T 12-Spd Chainring\nShimano MT-520 hydraulic 4-piston disc brakes, 203mm rotors\nX-Fusion Manic dropper post w/ 100/125mm travel\nKenda Nevegal 2 29\"/27.5\" 2.6\" TCS folding tires",
